    {
      "id": "ledger-notes",
      "kind": {
        "text": "`depends_on: F:nat-add-comm` is literal, not thematic: the two same-sign branches of the proof ARE `Nat.add_comm` transported through `Int.ofNat` and `Int.negSucc`. The two mixed-sign branches need no argument at all -- `Int.add` was defined so that `ofNat m + negSucc n` and `negSucc n + ofNat m` are literally the same term `Int.subNatNat m (succ n)`, so `Eq.refl` closes them. formal.statement is `Kernel::render_lean` of the admitted type, verbatim from `int_theorem_inventory`.",
        "type": "prose"
      },
